          <h2>From Figma to Accessible Code</h2>

          <p>Your design should reach the browser the way you designed it. I implement layouts pixel-precisely where it matters and flexibly where screens differ, and I raise questions early instead of quietly simplifying a design.</p>

          <p>Accessibility starts in the design file. Before development starts, I check colour contrast, focus and hover states, text sizes and the order of content, and I suggest small changes that keep your visual concept intact. This saves expensive corrections later and helps your clients comply with the law.</p>

          <h2>How We Work Together</h2>
          <ol>
            <li>A short introductory call about your studio, your clients and your typical projects.</li>
            <li>A small pilot project, such as a single page, a fix or an audit, so we can get to know each other's way of working.</li>
            <li>An estimate or fixed-price offer for each project, so you can calculate your own offer reliably.</li>
            <li>A preview server for intermediate results that you can share with your client.</li>
            <li>A clean handover with documentation, so that you or another developer can continue the work.</li>
          </ol>

          <h2>Pricing for Agencies</h2>

          <p>I invoice your agency or studio directly, by the hour, by the day or at a fixed price. My regular rates are listed on my homepage. If you book a monthly budget of hours, we can agree on a partner rate.</p>

        </article>

        <div class="cta-container">
          <a href="../#contact" class="buttonlike contact-link">request a pilot project</a>
        </div>

        <p>&nbsp;</p>

      </section>

      <section class="text-content-color" id="faq">
        <article class="text-content-layout text-width mb0">
          <h2>Working with Agencies and Studios: Questions and Answers</h2>
        </article>

        <article class="alternating-div-color text-content-layout-children">
          <div class="text-width-children mb0">
            <h3>Who owns the client relationship?</h3>
            <p>You do. I don't approach your clients on my own initiative, and I don't take on projects from your clients without your consent. We can put this in writing.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="text-width-children mb0">
            <h3>Do you talk to our clients directly?</h3>
            <p>Only if you want me to. Some studios prefer to handle all communication themselves, others bring me into technical meetings as part of their team. Both work for me.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="text-width-children mb0">
            <h3>Will you sign a non-disclosure agreement?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Confidentiality is part of white-label work, and I'm happy to sign your NDA or provide my own.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="text-width-children mb0">
            <h3>Which design handover do you need?</h3>
            <p>Figma, Sketch, Adobe XD or a PDF are all fine. Helpful additions are colour and font definitions, component states (hover, focus, error), and layouts for at least mobile and desktop. If anything is missing, I'll ask before guessing.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="text-width-children mb0">
            <h3>Which technologies and content management systems do you use?</h3>
            <p>Mostly WordPress, WooCommerce, Shopware 6, Astro, Eleventy and React, with HTML, CSS, TypeScript and JavaScript. Find all details on my <a href="/services/">skills and services</a> page.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="text-width-children mb0">
            <h3>Do we need to be based in Berlin?</h3>
            <p>No. I work with agencies and studios across Germany, Austria and Switzerland, mostly remotely. If you are in Berlin, we can also meet in person: find out more about my work as a <a href="/services/freelance-webdeveloper-berlin.html">freelance web developer in Berlin</a>.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="text-width-children mb0">
            <h3>Can we start with a small project?</h3>
            <p>Yes, that's what I recommend. A small first project shows us both whether the collaboration works, before you rely on me for a larger client project.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="text-width-children mb0 no-alternating-color">
            <h2>Let's Get to Know Each Other</h2>
            <p>Our first conversation is free of charge and without obligation.</p>
            <p>
              Tell me about your studio, and I will get back to you!
            </p>
          </div>

        </article>
